surface-warden
==============

This project derives from kernel-surface-ledger
(https://github.com/RajvardhanPatil07/kernel-surface-ledger), MIT License,
by the same author.

Provenance
----------

The first commit in this repository (094185cd) is an unmodified import of
kernel-surface-ledger at commit 0b77472. Everything in that commit predates
the micro1 Frontier Engineering Challenge and was NOT built for it:

  - collector/   read-only Linux evidence collection
  - engine/      deterministic reachability, attribution, set-cover planning
  - artifacts/   deterministic artifact templates
  - explain/     optional narration layer
  - web/         dashboard
  - data/        curated weights and CVE map
  - report.schema.json, fixtures/, and the tests covering the above

Everything after that commit was built during the competition window
(28-31 August 2026). To see exactly what was added, diff against the import
commit:

    git log --oneline 094185cd..HEAD
    git diff --stat 094185cd..HEAD

The competition work is: the evidence-acquisition agent (agent/), the static
checklist baseline (baseline/), the evaluation harness (evaluation/), the
replayable evidence timeline (fixtures/timeline-demo.json), the warden CLI,
the Makefile, and the documentation in docs/.

For convenience the boundary can also be tagged, after which
`pre-competition-baseline..HEAD` works in place of `094185cd..HEAD`:

    git tag -a pre-competition-baseline 094185cd \
      -m "Unmodified import of kernel-surface-ledger@0b77472"
    git push origin pre-competition-baseline

Verifying the import
--------------------

Commit 094185cd is timestamped 2026-08-28T15:43Z, which is after the
challenge kickoff, because that is when the copy was made. Its *contents*
are byte-identical to kernel-surface-ledger at 0b77472, which predates the
challenge. That claim is checkable rather than asserted:

    git clone https://github.com/RajvardhanPatil07/kernel-surface-ledger /tmp/ksl
    git -C /tmp/ksl checkout 0b77472
    git clone https://github.com/RajvardhanPatil07/surface-warden /tmp/sw
    git -C /tmp/sw checkout 094185cd
    diff -r --exclude=.git /tmp/ksl /tmp/sw

The engine is unchanged by the competition work: report.schema.json is a
frozen contract, and all new outputs are written to separate paths
(artifacts/runs/, artifacts/evaluation/).

